            <ArticleTitle>Interprocedural interval as a predictor of stent restenosis after previous coronary angioplasty. The Palmaz-Schatz Stent Investigators.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>683-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery stent implantation is used increasingly to treat restenosis after balloon angioplasty. This study demonstrates that a short interprocedural interval, between initial angioplasty and stent implantation, is a significant risk factor for in-stent restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
